 "traps": [
  "each .csproj is a unit named after its file; frameworks are per project, so ASP.NET Core belongs to the three Web projects (Sdk Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web) and to the ServiceDefaults projects through FrameworkReference Microsoft.AspNetCore.App",
  "versions live in Directory.Packages.props (central package management) at the root, in MinimalClean/ and in sample/: the PackageReference lines in the projects carry no version",
  "Aspire is an MSBuild SDK (Aspire.AppHost.Sdk) in the AppHost projects and a property (IsAspireSharedProject) in ServiceDefaults, not a package of those projects",
  "SQL Server and the Papercut SMTP container are declared in C# by the Aspire AppHost (AddSqlServer, AddContainer), not in a compose file",
  "SQLite is the fallback connection string when the app runs outside Aspire; Azure Application Insights is a Serilog sink package of the sample's Web project whose configuration is commented out",
  "xUnit is the test framework of the seven test projects (xunit.v3.mtp-off); Shouldly and NSubstitute are assertion and mocking libraries and are not listed, nor are Mediator, Serilog, FluentValidation and Vogen",
  "the repository is also a dotnet new template (.template.config): template symbols can remove projects when the template is instantiated",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
